{
  "title": "wgpu browser input wire",
  "why": "One row per input the wgpu browser shell admits, pinned across all three hops it crosses: the DOM event a listener on #semio-wgpu-canvas observes, the wire event the UI isolate transfers to the frame Worker, and the DispatchEvent the Worker projects it onto before Ui::dispatch_event sees it. Pointer and wheel rows carry their required event-time modifier snapshot so gestures remain correct when a modifier was pressed outside the renderer root or released between coalesced samples. Coordinates are NOT scaled (offset* are CSS pixels and the renderer lays out, hit-tests and paints in the same logical pixels — only a resize carries the physical surface extent plus its dpr), the wire spells its fields in camelCase while Rust spells them in snake_case, and button is a name, not a DOM integer.",
  "consumers": [
    "🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/📺️renderer/🧑‍🎨engine/🧪️tests/🎮️wgpu-browser-input-wire/🦀️.rs",
